{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates","id":1212718,"title":"In a World of Darkness... Murder Rates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-28T10:49:01-07:00","id":1212718,"title":"In a World of Darkness... Murder Rates","content":"In a World of Darkness what are the average crime rates? In a world with vampires what are the homicide rates? In the real world - Caracas, Venezuela has held on to its spot as the world's most dangerous city with a murder rate of 130.35 (that's per 100,000 people). Do any roleplaying groups actually figure out the murder rates in their settings? <br /> <br /> I get that ACTUAL numbers don't really matter necessarily, but description does matter. What would a city be like with a murder rate of 1,000 or 5,000 per 100,000 people? How would you describe it? There are a lot of factors involved, but I think it is interesting to think about. <br /> <br /> Just curious what other groups do in this regard?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T11:22:50-07:00","id":1212729,"title":"","content":"Considering I always described WoD ,minus the supernatural stuff's interference, as -0 earth I figured the numbers would be roughly the same. The big difference would be in the unreported ones, but my group isn't huge on looking up numbers for that sort of thing, so can't give exact figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:39:04-07:00","id":1212753,"title":"","content":"I feel like trying to ponder statistics on a subjective, theme-based and atmospheric make believe game is besides the point. Quiz your players over what amount would entail the darkest atmosphere, themes and subjects. The normal statistics for crime are quite depressing as they are in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:44:16-07:00","id":1212754,"title":"","content":"Depends on multiple factors like the kind of supernatural influence the city has but usually i would duplicate the crime statistics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:47:29-07:00","id":1212756,"title":"","content":"I don't think the statistics matter per se, but the cause for some of those crimes will be heavily influenced by the secret societies in your setting. No one can really interact with a setting in such a fashion as to make every disappearance victim by vampiric hunger or Sharta infestation count. Statistics are impersonal: they're stuff that &quot;happens to other people&quot;. Not something you want to focus on a game about personal horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:06:34-07:00","id":1212808,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure they have ghouls fulling spots as coroners, city hall officals, prosectucion, judges and poilce to make sure law goes in their favor and if too many bodies end up getting announced dominate some mortal and make them deranged so they can be fall guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","name":"flazeo25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:14:30-07:00","id":1212810,"title":"","content":"I actually have the murder rates be lower but the disappearances and the unsolved crimes higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T17:49:54-07:00","id":1212857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>flazeo25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates?p=1212808#post1212808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure they have ghouls fulling spots as coroners, city hall officals, prosectucion, judges and poilce to make sure law goes in their favor and if too many bodies end up getting announced dominate some mortal and make them deranged so they can be fall guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Damnation City went over why Kindred refrained from actually making thralls of high exposure public figures (said exposure), instead they go for the aides and advisors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:14:40-07:00","id":1213915,"title":"","content":"I think the world being shitty by itself is an oWoD thing, in CofD the world by itself is no more fucked up than ours, it's just the presence of supernaturals like vampires which makes it worse<br /> <br /> So the number of murders stays largely the same + the number of strange exsanguinated corpses that disappear off documents and statistics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T16:52:42-07:00","id":1213967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates?p=1212857#post1212857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Damnation City went over why Kindred refrained from actually making thralls of high exposure public figures (said exposure), instead they go for the aides and advisors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the 2nd edition Invictus DOES go after the high profile people for shits and giggles as well as demonstrate how adept they are at preserving the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T17:03:30-07:00","id":1213970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates?p=1213967#post1213967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the 2nd edition Invictus DOES go after the high profile people for shits and giggles as well as demonstrate how adept they are at preserving the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a game* you only play when you know you can win. Stars need to align or shit tons of planning need to go into making that little display of power go off without a hitch.<br /> <br /> The Invictus perform this practice occasionally to make a point. It's not something they allow to be a habit. It's not indicative of a persistent &quot;way things are.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Speaking in-game from the Invictus point of view, not of the game itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T19:06:02-07:00","id":1214007,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a ritual they enact to prove their relevance to the other four covenants because, from an in-game perspective, it\u2019s the \u201conly\u201d thing they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T20:29:39-07:00","id":1214027,"title":"","content":"Ultimately you need deaths and disappearances to be higher than the real world but low enough that no one questions it. Make it worse, but not so bad that population growth over the last century wouldn't be possible.<br /> Everyone is saying statistics don't matter, but if you want to make them matter, then that would be my advise--your rates should be low enough that you somehow still got to 7 billion humans by 2001. Keep population growth relatively the same. Less people are perhaps dying of old age, but people aren't having more kids to keep up, cuz that would give off the masquerade if people were deliberately having more kids to compensate for the unknown deaths. Compare to 300 years ago in which people had lots of kids to cope with accidents and diseases, but in the modern day, a lot of people going missing and population fluctuating would stick out.<br /> Your statistic should not heavily impact population growths. Anyway, hope that is helpful too ;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T02:07:14-07:00","id":1214084,"title":"","content":"Murder rates is a start, but surely lacking in explaining things. Statistics about missing people and the like needs to come into the calculation as well. But even then you need to consider where the chronicle takes place. Sure there's no problem with the right feel of danger in the night in Honduras or the slums of S\u00e3o Paulo, but for most countires in the EU it's stretching it by plainly saying our world but with supernaturals. Surely it's a premise to the setting but take a look at one splat book and you realize that if you count for half of one splats killings/kidnappings/etc there's just not possible for quite a few countries in the world let alone if you try to stay close to the actual setting with most splats and other things going bump in the night. <br /> It takes a fair bit of suspension of disbelief to accept that spirits/claimed/vampires/mages/demons/ghost/horrors/werewolves/etc.etc. goes bump in the night.<br /> Maybe it works better if you are more used to the idea that kidnappings and or murder rates are higher, like the US capital of Washington DC seems like crazy to me if i check the murder rates per capita against my home of Sweden, which is about 1/10 of the rates of DC. And the last few years, gang criminality has gone up and the use of deadly force by them has become way more common today then for a few years back, but still every murder is still extremely newsworthy and get's attention beyond what would be possible of there was ~1500 homicides instead of the 113 we had last year. Our neighbour, Norway has about half of our, Swedens, murder rate, sadly one year, 2011, this number got to about the same rate as Sweden, by one act of terrorism. This massacre tells a lot of how bad a representation statistics can be if you don't know about them, and tells nothing of how safe from being killed you are in Norway for instance if you look at the 2011 statistics instead of any other year.<br /> <br /> So in all this, we at our table start by figuring out the general feel of the place we play in and go from there, accepting that our chronicle will diverge from reality one way or another. For instance the current chronicle is taking place in the city of Catania in Sicily. Italy, a pretty safe place over all but we want to push up the crime and gonzo factor so in our chronicle the city has become a hub of criminal war, forcing the Cosa Nostra to defend itself from foreign crime syndicates trying to get a stronger hold as the main &quot;cover up&quot; for how bad the city is before calculating in supernaturals. The feel I'm pretty sure is way closer to the Mafia wars a few decades ago then it is right now, but that's a feel we're looking for in this particular chronicle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:55:29-07:00","id":1214246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates?p=1213967#post1213967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the 2nd edition Invictus DOES go after the high profile people for shits and giggles as well as demonstrate how adept they are at preserving the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just too much attention honestly, vampires infiltrate high society the most to marginally influence mortal policies and politics to protect themselves. They ghoul the guy doing the paper work at the police station rather than the chief of police, make a thrall out of the wife of the governor or the secretary of a corporate CEO, it's all about subtle influence so they don't attract attention to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T17:30:52-07:00","id":1214369,"title":"","content":"The stereotype of them has them sitting directly on the executive board of some corporation with a routine of fucking with the current CFO, secure in the knowledge that he won't go straight to the SEC, FBI, (or some other supernatural organization) instead. Now they can't possibly know that unless they were already controlling him or because they already have their claws in the relevant federal alphabet soups, effectively nullifying any threat to ensure the Masquerade stays mostly in tact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T19:17:37-07:00","id":1214395,"title":"","content":"Crime rates would be a lot higher, although that fact be kept off the official books, but I figure birth rates would also be higher thanks to creatures like lust and fertility spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T21:04:43-07:00","id":1214412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates?p=1214395#post1214395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crime rates would be a lot higher, although that fact be kept off the official books, but I figure birth rates would also be higher thanks to creatures like lust and fertility spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it\u2019s statistically a nice world to live in? That... actually makes sense. Never thought about it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T21:31:23-07:00","id":1214415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates?p=1214412#post1214412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it\u2019s statistically a nice world to live in? That... actually makes sense. Never thought about it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, depending on how you decide to take what books have said, it <i>can</i> be interpreted that sans the supernatural involvement, crimes and such would be lower than it is in the real world, since the phrasing at times makes it sound like the atrocity level as humanity experiences it is about the same but a portion of that is attributed to supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T00:08:23-07:00","id":1214451,"title":"","content":"In my head canon I retain the idea that it is our world, only darker, but the truth is I don't really depict it as any darker, I just rewrite real world events with a supernatural edge sometimes even borrowing them whole cloth from the news. For example I borrowed a public gang hit only now the targets and those behind the attack were involved in a war between supernatural groups. For the world at large nothing is changed, but the characters are now privy to the secrets underlying those events.<br /> <br /> As for a city with a murder rate of 1,000 per 100,000? You have a city where everyone knows someone who was murdered, may have even witnessed a murder first hand. What you would have is a city where everyone lives in fear, a place where people don't go out alone after dark and they panic at the sight of every hoody. Like a zombie apocalypse I can't see how such a city could be used for more than a one shot story. Rational deniability of the darkness is kind of needed to keep the wheels turning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T10:33:16-07:00","id":1214671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212718-in-a-world-of-darkness-murder-rates?p=1214451#post1214451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my head canon I retain the idea that it is our world, only darker, but the truth is I don't really depict it as any darker, I just rewrite real world events with a supernatural edge sometimes even borrowing them whole cloth from the news. For example I borrowed a public gang hit only now the targets and those behind the attack were involved in a war between supernatural groups. For the world at large nothing is changed, but the characters are now privy to the secrets underlying those events.<br /> <br /> As for a city with a murder rate of 1,000 per 100,000? You have a city where everyone knows someone who was murdered, may have even witnessed a murder first hand. What you would have is a city where everyone lives in fear, a place where people don't go out alone after dark and they panic at the sight of every hoody. Like a zombie apocalypse I can't see how such a city could be used for more than a one shot story. Rational deniability of the darkness is kind of needed to keep the wheels turning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, 1.000 in every 100.000 is ridiculous. In contrast, here are some of the real world homicide statistics for the year 2017:<br /> <br /> <b>London:</b><br /> Population: 8,7m<br /> Homicides: 130<br /> Per 100k: 1,4<br /> <br /> <b>New York City:</b><br /> Population: 8,6m<br /> Homicides: 290<br /> Per 100k: 3,3<br /> <br /> <b>Chicago:</b><br /> Population: 2,6m<br /> Homicides: 620<br /> Per 100k: 23,8<br /> <br /> <b>Detroit City:</b><br /> Population: 0,7m<br /> Homicides: 290<br /> Per 100k: 43,4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T13:44:02-07:00","id":1214750,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind also the missing persons stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T13:52:53-07:00","id":1214754,"title":"","content":"There is also the dark figure of crime to consider. Crime statistics are often estimated to twice the reported rate. Also, you should consider aggravated assault, and other violent felonies, not just murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T13:59:57-07:00","id":1214762,"title":"","content":"Yeah a lot of the ways supernaturals kill people would potentially not turn up as murder. Anemia (all it takes is a lick and there's no wound), missing persons, spontaneous neck ruptures.<br /> <br /> I pondered this kind of thing before because it seems like whatever way you go can cause some drastic repercussions for the world. If the crime rates are the same, it implies that there's less 'our world' crimes, to make room for the supernatural stuff, which could further imply that people are less prone to committing crime (though as Chronicles points out people are more afraid of revelations and dark secrets, as the world isn't an inherently evil one, just full of mystery). If you adjust things with higher rates, that means you must have lower populations, or potentially much larger populations.<br /> <br /> In all honesty it's never come up, inside a game. This is the kind of thing that seems to be something a fan might know and talk about on forums but wouldn't really be brought up in the game anyways. Especially if you keep in mind the toolbox approach, where vampires may be entirely non-existent in a city like New York because they were wiped out in one game, while it may be the capitol of Vampire Enterprises in another and Johnny doesn't like vampires so they don't exist in his setting. When something similar comes up, it's easier to explain, for instance, 'That's a bad part of town, crime rates have skyrocketed since the Eclipse,' or 'the murder rates in Citytropolis are higher than usual for cities of its size.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:38:24-07:00","id":1214798,"title":"","content":"I leave the murder rates largely the same. But not all deaths by natural causes, freak accidents, or Darwin Awards candidates are accidents or natural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T03:40:00-07:00","id":1219221,"title":"","content":"I always went with the &quot;supernatural&quot; effects are easier to conceal - meaning a lot of real world accidents, Runaways, Missing Persons, and Cold Cases, are very well concealed Murders.<br /> <br /> If anything, if you're looking for vampire attacks where a lot of murders happen, you MAY be looking in the wrong place! All vampires have ways of turning murders into &quot;mistakes&quot;.<ul><li>Obfuscate and carry a corpse atop a building and let it drop, or Nightmare to make them jump out a window to &quot;saftey&quot; - pavement usually hides blood loss :P</li> <li>Use Nightmare to make a Victim &quot;run into traffic&quot;</li> <li>Majesty or Dominante a victim to get an assault rifle and open fire on a crowd - let the cops kill them for you (and while you're at it, grab a snack in the gunfire - bullet holes are more natural than invisible bite wounds!)</li> <li>Go &quot;Wild Shape&quot; protean and maul the body a bit. Let the coroner chalk it up to &quot;wild dog attack&quot;</li> <li>Use &quot;animalisim&quot; to summon a pack of rats and have them devour the corps.</li> <li>Don't use and Discipline - simply carry a Corpse under water with a shovel, dig a hole, and bury them. You don't need to breathe so stay under as long as you like!</li> </ul>Point is vampire Disciplines offer not just useful combat and espionage tricks, but also ways to clean up messes. Plus there are usually more than one vamp per city. If a Vampire starts leaving &quot;suspect corpses&quot; around, the police MAY find a pile of suspicious ashes besides some manacles, with a sharpened &quot;stake&quot; in the pile of ashes.<br /> <br /> Vampires regulate the masquerade cause they know IF people notice them, it can be tricky. But they know they need to feed. So better to maximize hiding bodies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}